From f33689fbcaa0c3c5d845edcfc6e71b37e890c3d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Damman <xdamman@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:29:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Belfry: applications from keys that are not relay members

With [groups] applicants = true, any signed-in key may send a join or leave
request (9021 / 9022) for a group that exists, and nothing else; the relay
owner may hand in such a request signed by someone else. A request from a
non-member, or tagged waitlist, never admits by itself: an admin decides.
At most 20 per key per hour.
